## §10. Audit Bus

Unchanged from v1.0. `f_m10_record_audit(st, corr_id, object_id, status, message, recommendation)` — a direct structural mirror of `f_m9_record_audit`/`f_m8_record_audit`: same `AuditResultInstance` shape, same `st.audit.*` counter increments per status branch, `module := "Module 10"` (free-text string field, no collision risk unlike the event-bus module-ID enum), same `AUDIT_SCHEMA_VERSION`.

| Outcome | Audit Status | Example message |
|---|---|---|
| Stage 1 geometry failure | `AUDIT_FAIL` | `"TradeRecommendation rejected: DEGENERATE_ZONE"` |
| Stage 1 ATR failure | `AUDIT_WARNING` | `"TradeRecommendation rejected: ATR_INVALID"` |
| Stage 3 RR failure | `AUDIT_WARNING` | `"TradeRecommendation rejected: RR_BELOW_MINIMUM"` |
| Stage 3 confidence failure | `AUDIT_WARNING` | `"TradeRecommendation rejected: CONFIDENCE_BELOW_MINIMUM"` |
| Stage 4 creation | `AUDIT_PASS` | `"TradeRecommendation created: <baseId>"` |
| Stage 5 SL_HIT | `AUDIT_PASS` | `"TradeRecommendation transitioned -> STOPPED (SL_HIT)"` |
| Stage 5 TP_HIT | `AUDIT_PASS` | `"TradeRecommendation transitioned -> FULFILLED (TP_HIT)"` |
| Stage 5 expiry | `AUDIT_PASS` | `"TradeRecommendation transitioned -> EXPIRED"` |
| Stage 0 dedup skip | *(none — steady-state no-op, not audited — see note below)* | — |
| Overflow eviction | `AUDIT_WARNING` | `"TradeRecommendation evicted on overflow, exitReason at eviction: <value or NONE>"` |

**Note on the dedup skip:** Module 8 and Module 9 both record one `AUDIT_SKIPPED` per duplicate-detected attempt. Module 10 does **not**, because — per §4.3 — Module 10's dedup key is marked on first *attempt*, not first *success*, so a "duplicate" can only mean "already attempted on a prior bar," which by construction never happens more than once per candidate (Stage 0 checks the key before Stage 1 runs, every bar, for every `TRIGGERED` candidate still resident in `g_m9_registry`) — there is structurally no repeated-attempt case left to skip and audit. This is called out explicitly as a deliberate divergence from the M8/M9 audit pattern, not an omission.

`AUDIT_SCHEMA_VERSION`, correlation ID convention (`"M10-" + str.tostring(bar_index)`), and `f_push_audit(g_audit_registry, ..., MAX_AUDIT_REGISTRY)` are used exactly as established by Modules 5–9, unmodified. (Note: `g_audit_registry` uses the frozen `f_push_audit` helper as-is — the C1 resolution in §8 applies only to `g_trade_rec_registry` and its four parallel arrays, not to the shared audit/event buses, which have no evicted-instance-inspection requirement and so present no equivalent contradiction.)

